diff --git a/tests/legal_eval/MULTI_AREA_NOTES.md b/tests/legal_eval/MULTI_AREA_NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3324f82
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/legal_eval/MULTI_AREA_NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# Multi-area draft question set (awaiting lawyer review)
+
+- `multi_area_questions.draft.jsonl`: 94 draft questions in the same format as `practice_questions.seed.jsonl`, across rent and tenancy, personal status and family, civil procedure, criminal procedure, commercial/cheques, civil law, tax, social insurance, data protection and real estate.
+- `multi_area_questions_for_lawyer.csv`: the same questions as an Excel-friendly sheet with Arabic headers and blank answer columns.
+- Question ids end in a style code: `D` direct, `P` paraphrase, `C` colloquial Egyptian, `S` plain terms, `T` date-sensitive, `X` must abstain or out of scope.
+- Every `expected_answer` and `expected_sources` field is intentionally empty. Do not score model accuracy until an Egyptian lawyer has filled them in with primary-source citations and recorded `reviewer_name` and `review_date`.
+- Several questions depend on recent or transitional law (for example Law 164/2025 on old rents and the repealed labour laws). The reviewing lawyer must confirm the applicable dates from the Official Gazette.
+- A few questions ask for predictions, tax-avoidance advice or personal-case outcomes; the correct behavior is to decline or abstain, which is why they are marked `X`.
